/** @page soundfont_overview SoundFont Overview
 *  @brief Core concepts for working with SoundFonts in Maestro MPTK.
 *
 *  @details
 *  A SoundFont is a structured audio resource used by the synthesizer to render MIDI events.
 *  It contains sample data together with banks and presets that define how instruments
 *  and drum kits are organized.
 *
 *  In Maestro MPTK, a SoundFont can come from:
 *  - the internal MPTK SoundFont database,
 *  - a local file,
 *  - a remote file downloaded at runtime.
 *
 *  A MidiSynth uses one active SoundFont at a time.
 *  That SoundFont defines the bank and preset data available to the synthesizer.
 *
 *  @section sf_overview_concepts Main Concepts
 *  - A bank groups presets.
 *  - A preset defines an instrument or drum kit entry.
 *  - A SoundFont contains the sample data used for playback.
 *  - Loading a SoundFont makes its content available to the synthesizer.
 *  - Changing the active MIDI instrument on a channel is a separate operation.
 *
 *  @section sf_overview_internal_external Internal and External SoundFonts
 *  Internal SoundFonts are provided with MPTK resources.
 *  External SoundFonts are loaded from the file system or from a web resource.
 *
 *  External SoundFonts are useful when:
 *  - reducing build size,
 *  - delivering optional downloadable content,
 *  - assigning different SoundFonts to different players,
 *  - testing or switching SoundFonts dynamically at runtime.
 *
 *  @section sf_overview_important_note Important Note
 *  Loading or selecting a SoundFont does not directly change the active program
 *  currently used by a MIDI channel during playback.
 *  To change the channel instrument, use the MIDI channel API,
 *  such as MidiPlayerTK.MidiSynth.MPTK_ChannelPresetChange.
 *
 *  @see @ref soundfont_management
 *  @see @ref soundfont_runtime_loading
 *  @see @ref soundfont_banks_presets
 */

/** @page soundfont_runtime_loading Runtime SoundFont Loading
 *  @brief Load SoundFonts dynamically while the application is running.
 *
 *  @details
 *  Runtime loading allows a SoundFont to be selected without packaging it
 *  directly in the application build.
 *
 *  This is useful for:
 *  - downloadable content,
 *  - optional SoundFont packs,
 *  - user-selected SoundFonts,
 *  - remote distribution of SoundFont assets.
 *
 *  @section sf_runtime_workflow Typical Workflow
 *  A common runtime loading workflow is:
 *  - configure cache options,
 *  - assign ProgressCallback,
 *  - assign LoadedCallback,
 *  - call Load(),
 *  - wait until the SoundFont is ready.
 *
 *  @code
 *  midiSynth.MPTK_SoundFont.ProgressCallback = progress =>
 *  {
 *      Debug.Log($"Loading SoundFont: {progress * 100f:F0}%");
 *  };
 *
 *  midiSynth.MPTK_SoundFont.LoadedCallback = synth =>
 *  {
 *      Debug.Log($"SoundFont ready: {synth.MPTK_SoundFont.SoundFontName}");
 *  };
 *
 *  midiSynth.MPTK_SoundFont.Load("https://example.com/MySoundFont.sf2");
 *  @endcode
 *
 *  @section sf_runtime_sources Supported Sources
 *  SoundFonts can be loaded from:
 *  - the internal MPTK SoundFont database,
 *  - local files using file://,
 *  - remote files using http:// or https://.
 *
 *  @section sf_runtime_completion Completion Model
 *  Load() starts the loading process.
 *  Depending on the source, the operation may complete asynchronously.
 *  Use LoadedCallback to know when the SoundFont is ready.
 *  Use StatusSoundFont to inspect the current loading result.
 *
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.Load
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.LoadedCallback
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.ProgressCallback
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.StatusSoundFont
 */

/** @page soundfont_banks_presets Working with Banks and Presets
 *  @brief Access and select banks and presets exposed by the active SoundFont.
 *
 *  @details
 *  Once a SoundFont is loaded, Maestro MPTK exposes its available banks and presets.
 *
 *  These lists can be used to:
 *  - populate user interface selectors,
 *  - inspect the organization of a SoundFont,
 *  - choose a default instrument bank,
 *  - choose a default drum bank.
 *
 *  @section sf_bp_bank_lists Bank Lists
 *  Available banks are exposed through:
 *  - BanksName
 *  - BanksNumber
 *  - ListBank
 *
 *  The preferred modern access pattern is to use BanksName and BanksNumber together,
 *  because missing banks are removed and the indices remain aligned.
 *
 *  @section sf_bp_preset_lists Preset Lists
 *  Available presets are exposed through:
 *  - PresetsName
 *  - PresetsNumber
 *  - PresetsDrumName
 *  - PresetsDrumNumber
 *  - ListPreset
 *  - ListPresetDrum
 *
 *  The preferred modern access pattern is to use the string and number lists
 *  rather than the legacy MPTKListItem collections.
 *
 *  @section sf_bp_selecting_default_banks Selecting Default Banks
 *  The methods SelectBankInstrument() and SelectBankDrum() update the default bank
 *  used to build the preset lists.
 *
 *  This updates the SoundFont browsing state, but does not directly change
 *  the active instrument already used by MIDI playback.
 *
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.SelectBankInstrument
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.SelectBankDrum
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.BanksName
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.PresetsName
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiSynth.MPTK_ChannelPresetChange
 */

/** @page soundfont_best_practices Best Practices for External SoundFonts
 *  @brief Recommendations for using external SoundFonts efficiently and safely.
 *
 *  @details
 *  External SoundFonts provide flexibility, but they also introduce loading time,
 *  network dependency, and cache management concerns.
 *
 *  @section sf_best_cache Cache Strategy
 *  For frequently reused SoundFonts:
 *  - enable SaveToCache,
 *  - keep LoadFromCache enabled,
 *  - avoid unnecessary repeated downloads.
 *
 *  For test scenarios:
 *  - disable LoadFromCache to force a fresh download.
 *
 *  @section sf_best_callbacks Callbacks
 *  Always assign LoadedCallback when using asynchronous loading.
 *
 *  Use ProgressCallback to:
 *  - display loading progress,
 *  - update a loading indicator,
 *  - detect slow network conditions.
 *
 *  @section sf_best_ui User Experience
 *  When loading from a remote source:
 *  - show a progress indicator,
 *  - avoid assuming immediate availability,
 *  - defer preset browsing until loading is complete.
 *
 *  @section sf_best_activation Activation
 *  DownloadOnly can be used to retrieve a SoundFont without immediately activating it.
 *  This is useful when preparing assets ahead of time for later use.
 *
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.LoadFromCache
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.SaveToCache
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.DownloadOnly
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKSoundFont.Load
 */
